/*****************************************************************************
    jitJ1 -- RUNG 1 OF THE jitLadder. 2026-07-31.

        assign + arithmetic + tail return, fired at TWO inputs.

    THE LADDER'S PURPOSE, in one sentence: nothing in this tree has ever
    asserted that an ACTION, jitted end to end, RETURNS THE INTENDED VALUE.
    `jitPop.sh` asserts the if/else block topology; the Phase-1 tables assert
    individual operators through a scratch driver. The spine -- build an action,
    fire it, get the right answer -- was missing, and J1 is it.

    Each rung is the previous rung plus ONE construct, so a red NAMES the
    construct instead of handing you a haystack. That is the genLadder lesson
    applied to the JIT, which is the one subsystem that never had it.

    ============================================================================
    ⚠⚠ THE MANDATORY CRITERION, AND IT IS NOT "THE ANSWER IS RIGHT"

    A right answer does not prove the COMPILED CODE produced it.

    Under jitting the interpreter executes the action body FOR REAL at emit time
    (docs/jit.md S2.2 -- a jitted `print` printed `hello world` DURING
    compilation). So an end-to-end POP can go green because the INTERPRETER did
    the work while compiling, with the compiled function returning a baked
    constant. Right answer, wrong universe, exit 0 the whole way.

    So every rung COMPILES ONCE AND FIRES TWICE, with the input changed AFTER
    emission:

        jaIn = 10;  testing(jitJ1);   -> jaOut must be 15
        jaIn = 30;  jitRefire();      -> jaOut must be 35   <-- THE PROOF

    Row 2 recompiles NOTHING. If its answer tracks the new input, the
    computation happened at RUN TIME in compiled code -- there is no other
    explanation. If jaOut stays 15, the emitter FOLDED the input at compile time
    and row 1 was theatre. This is the load-vs-fold distinction jit.md has
    listed as unobservable since Phase 1; jitRefire is what makes it observable.

    SECOND CRITERION: `jitDegrade count = 0`. J1 claims full coverage of its own
    constructs, so nothing in it may silently fall through to emit-time
    interpretation. The degrade counter stops being only a crossover burn-down
    and becomes a per-rung assertion.
    ============================================================================

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT (standing harness rule H2).
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(JitLadder);
define
    jaIn;
    jaOut;
    /*  The whole rung: one assign, one arithmetic op, value left in a field.
        Deliberately the smallest thing that still needs the FULL scaffold --
        seed a field operand, emit the add, store back, cap the function, hand
        it to ORC, look the symbol up, and call it.  */
    jitJ1 code={ jaOut = jaIn + 5; };
    ;

jaIn  = 10;
jaOut = 0;
print "J1 fire 1 setup : jaIn =" jaIn:;
testing(jitJ1);
print "J1 fire 1 result: jaOut =" jaOut " (want 15)":;

/*  ⚠ NO RECOMPILE BELOW THIS LINE. Only the input changes.  */
jaIn  = 30;
jaOut = 0;
print "J1 fire 2 setup : jaIn =" jaIn " (recompile: NONE)":;
jitRefire();
print "J1 fire 2 result: jaOut =" jaOut " (want 35; 15 = FOLDED at compile time; 0 = never fired)":;

print "J1 SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
